WEBVTT

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:47.770
<b>K & C Pharmaceutical Corporation, Japan</b>

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.700
Target appears to be heading south.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.660
Her footprints were found 
400 meters south of here.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.250
All vehicles are searching the area.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.290
I'll appraise you, as new 
information is available.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.190
Director...

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:13.410
Our surveillance cameras alone 
can't cover it any further.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.550
Use government and police 
cameras, as well.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:27.170
Damn it!

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.310
This is too slow...

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.060
Too slow!

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.760
<i>Target may have left the research 
facility's surveillance area.</i>

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.920
<i>It may take time for street-surveillance 
cameras to find her.</i>

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:47.330
<i>If the situation changes, 
contact me immediately.</i>

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.630
Over.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:49.710
<i>Roger.</i>

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.370
Director...

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.450
Could the target have possibly 
jumped even farther?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:01.960
Why do you think I limit her 
calorie intake at dinner?

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.020
We'll get some good data today.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.710
I want to see how far the Queen can go

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.030
on that amount.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.670
Yes! Here we go!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.340
Ugh... Not again.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.140
This is why I requested a bigger budget!

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.980
Target located on the national highway,

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.060
500 meters southeast.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.990
Since it's a street-surveillance camera, 
this is the best it can do.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:58.610
All vehicles, surround the area 
in which the target is located.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.420
<i>Car #4, proceed directly to the point.</i>

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.970
<i>She may have one more jump in her,</i>

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.200
<i>but the distance won't be too great.</i>

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.330
Yes! Analysis complete!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.830
Sending coordinates!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.490
Car #4 here.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.190
Minnie C. is heading toward the target.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:44.660
<i>Roger.</i>

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.200
<i>You can wait where you are.</i>

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:55.920
So cold...

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:00.540
Is this how all of the outside world is?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.260
Where do you think you're going,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.590
Red Queen?

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.760
Don't come near me!

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:12.800
Stop being stubborn, and return 
to where it is nice and warm.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.080
No!

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.590
Everyone is waiting for you.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.440
Open!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.030
You see?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.620
You have already exhausted your energy.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.790
Wonderland is the only place you belong.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.260
Who's there?

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.290
I see.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:30.680
#106.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.800
She appears to be resisting.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.600
That's the Red Queen for you.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.200
I'm impressed she had 
that much power left.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.160
No.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.090
Huh?

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.880
This is

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.620
someone else?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.790
Jump.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.070
Visualize the largest town you can.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:26.530
Go there and cause as much 
commotion as you can.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.740
Who are you?

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:31.870
We'll meet again.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.010
What?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:58.980
What happened?

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.300
I don't know!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.100
Perhaps a lightning strike.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.670
We'll switch to another 
channel and restart it.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.430
Lightning?

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.400
All right! Success!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.710
Restoring monitors.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:22.880
Where's the target?

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.590
I don't see her.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.800
Nothing here, either.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.260
<i>Tachibana here.</i>

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:33.220
Capture of the Red Queen has failed.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.970
Someone interfered.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.150
<i>Who was it?</i>

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.520
I don't know.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.180
A female ability-user I have never seen.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.820
She told the Red Queen

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.900
to go to a large town and 
cause a commotion.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.630
<i>To all vehicles.</i>

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:50.530
<i>All cars, except #4, expand search 
to the metropolitan area.</i>

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:51.490
Roger.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:56.070
<i>Do whatever you can to pick up her trail.</i>

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.590
All vehicles have changed course.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:02.960
They're heading south, 
toward the metro area.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.590
<i>Director, further pursuit is impossible.</i>

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.430
Why?

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:10.980
The bridge...

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.590
The bridge... is gone.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.610
All vehicles, return to the research facility.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.790
Minnie C., as soon as you arrive, 
report in detail.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:34.910
Over.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:40.830
Go to a large town and 
cause a commotion...

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.580
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.640
<i>Alice,</i>

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:48.110
<i>having drifted in space for a long time,</i>

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.660
<i>began to feel a bit dizzy.</i>

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:54.060
<i>When she knew she was 
capable of walking again,</i>

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.610
<i>she felt relieved.</i>

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.280
<i>"If I can get to the top of that hill,"</i>

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.550
<i>thought Alice,</i>

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:07.940
<i>"I'll have a much better 
view of the garden."</i>

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:36.970
<b>The Red Queen Escapes</b>

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.250
Sorry to wake you so early.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.910
If you're tired, you can sleep now.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.010
Okay.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.100
<i>Target located.</i>

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.540
<i>She's in Shinjuku.</i>

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.450
<i>Cameras spotted her at 4:57 AM.</i>

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:38.220
Send the footage of the target to me.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.320
<i>Roger.</i>

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.160
<b>You Have a New Message</b>

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.440
Indeed,

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.540
that certainly is a large town...

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.140
Here is your order.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:15.520
Truly, you do fantastic work!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.090
I was right to ask you for 
this, Kashimura-san.

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.050
Is that so?

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:25.420
That's a lot.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:26.950
It's to thank you.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.190
Consider it a token of my gratitude.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:33.040
I accepted this job because 
it was a personal request.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.110
I won't get buddy-buddy with you people.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.190
Hey, old man!

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.790
Who do you think you're address—

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:39.130
Shut up!

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.180
Sorry about that.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:43.550
He can be a bit hot-headed.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.280
I'll accept my fee and nothing more.

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:49.730
Kashimura-san...

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.810
You really are a strange one, aren't you?

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.110
Thank you for coming!

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.780
<b>Sawaki Industries</b>

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.460
<b>Comprehensive, Superior Information 

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.500
Welcome.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:20.880
Oh, Kashimura-san...

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.760
Haven't seen you in a while.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.890
Cigarettes. The usual.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.850
You should quit smoking.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.210
It'll kill you, Kashimura-san.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.290
Shut it.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:33.590
Kashimura-san, Kashimura-san...

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:35.650
I'm worried about that girl.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.860
Would you take her to the police?

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.780
She's been there for three hours.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:46.130
A child shouldn't be in Kabukicho.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.480
Tell the police.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:50.860
I called, but they wouldn't do anything.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.160
They don't trust foreigners.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.910
<b>Check Screen and Touch to Continue 
Are you 20 or older? 

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.910
Ask the owner to, then.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.270
I can't!

00:12:55.270 --> 00:12:57.450
The owner hates police.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:13:00.630
Also, he's been stealing donation money.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.380
<b>Donation Box 
Your Cooperation Is Appreciated</b>

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.380
He's a bad man.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.590
Hey, little girl.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.680
You aren't supposed to 
touch the merchandise.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:16.140
If you're lost, why don't 
I take you home?

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.610
Have you and I met before?

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.360
Kashimura Zoroku.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.610
Born June 19, 1943.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:31.590
One granddaughter named Sanae.

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:35.040
She's been at training camp for her 
high school club since yesterday.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:39.810
But I don't know what "club" 
and "training camp" mean.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:41.770
Guess I was wrong.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.050
But you don't seem like a bad person.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.490
Hey, you!

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:49.900
How would you like to 
make a deal with me?

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.350
A deal?

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.050
If you agree,

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:55.430
I'll grant any wish you want!

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.600
What the heck is this?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.190
Something from a manga?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.460
Sorry, but I don't know 
much about that stuff.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.250
Huh?

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.690
I... I get it.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.380
You're making fun of me, right?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.290
I'm not making fun of you.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.450
I just have no clue what you're saying.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.130
Forget it!

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.630
What was that?

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.450
She disappeared, Kashimura-san!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.050
Kashimura-san, what's going on?

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.050
<b>Land for Sale</b>

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.050
No idea.

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:38.900
This is bad.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.650
My power's weakening.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:46.140
I'll have to go with the guy from before...

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.660
<i>Thank you for your patronage.</i>

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:03.380
Hey, you...

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.130
You really won't make a deal with me?

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.790
How did you get in this car?

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.550
Don't worry about that.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:15.710
What's your name, little girl?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.140
Where is your home?

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.530
I have no home.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:23.560
C-Come on!

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.900
Make a deal with me.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.020
If you do, I'll grant any wish you want.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:31.280
Is this the attitude you take when 
you ask someone for something?

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.480
If you have something to say, 
have the right attitude—

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:36.700
Hesitate, and you'll die.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:37.950
What?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.110
Look ahead.

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.470
What was that about?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.660
Just get out of here!

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:57.720
It'll come back!

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.220
Tch!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.720
I missed...

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.310
Onee-sama, don't you think 
this is going a bit far—

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.800
Shoot, Yonaga!

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.640
But...

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:05.560
Don't argue!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.780
Right now!

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:09.690
O-Okay...

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.750
No need for mercy.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.980
I-I'll have to try my best to miss.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:15.620
Just shoot right into it!

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.660
What is that?

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:31.300
The sisters who followed me.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.890
The younger can call a bow, while the 
older can call anything with a chain.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.350
Like the wrecking ball before, 
and that bike, too.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.360
There's no chain on a bike.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:41.310
Yes, there is.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.290
The bike chain!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.110
Don't slow now.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.030
They'll be on us again soon!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:00.590
Ow...

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:02.500
Hey, why did you stop?

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.670
Get out.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:06.790
You know those two girls, right?

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.820
Don't drag a stranger into your problems.

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:09.880
I don't need that.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:11.880
I think I like you.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:21.620
Darn it!

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.170
We're too conspicuous...

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.910
I missed again!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:26.550
Yonaga, hurry up and shoot again!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.940
O-Open.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.200
T-Try to miss.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.780
Try to miss...

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.570
Wh-What the hell are you doing?

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.950
I'll drive!

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.450
Hey! Stop!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.920
P-Please stop, Sa-chan!

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:01.800
You did it, Yonaga!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.140
Sa-chan...

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.400
What was that?

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.710
Should we call the police?

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:14.310
No, I'd say an ambulance.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.580
What the hell is going on?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.260
Foreigners?

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.370
Are they filming a movie?

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.620
Was that CG?

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.510
You can't get away now, Red Queen!

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:30.980
They ordered you to follow me here,

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.210
you useless sisters?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:33.990
U-Useless?!

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.010
Onee-sama, calm down.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:39.080
Sa-chan, let's return to 
the research facility.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:43.270
I... I know they conduct some 
unpleasant tests.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:47.080
B-But we cannot live in the outside world!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.010
That's a lie!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:52.520
I won't be fooled anymore, 
and I'm done being a lab rat.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:55.110
I'll crush that place with my own hands.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.960
S-Sa-chan...

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:00.240
You don't know anything 
about the outside world!

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:03.710
Yonaga, shoot her!

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:04.410
Huh?

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.740
I won't go back.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.360
Sa-chan...

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.620
Sa-chan...

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.730
I'm sorry!

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:18.930
Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.260
You think that

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:21.820
pointing that dangerous thing 
at people is all right?

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.170
Wh-What are you doing—

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:40.160
That's what I'd like to know.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:40.670
Ow, ow...

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:43.360
What are you doing, 
in the middle of the city?

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.750
Do you know how many people 
could have been hurt

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.290
by one wrong move in your 
nonsensical game of tag?

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.460
Take a good look at what you've done!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.380
Think you're playing a video game?!

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.370
Huh?

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.090
And as for you two!

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:57.460
Y-Yes?

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.830
Do you two have a beef 
with me or something?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.020
N-No...

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:03.050
N-Not at all...

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.030
Listen to me.

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:07.290
This world has boundaries 
you must respect.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:09.460
I don't know what you three 
have been through,

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:12.310
but old folks and children 
walk around these parts.

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:16.830
Your actions could have killed someone.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:19.290
Listen up.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:21.240
The police will be here soon.

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:24.490
You're gonna have to step up and 
atone for what you've done.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.340
What do you say?

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:28.860
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:39.550
<b>Yotsuya Police Station</b>

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:42.660
Okay, why don't you two 
give me your names?

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.120
Now, will you tell me your name?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.320
I don't mind telling you, but...

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.670
Are you hungry?

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:00.020
You expect me to believe 
that nonsense?!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:03.700
Plenty of witnesses were at the scene.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.270
Aren't they telling you the 
same "nonsense" I am?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.780
All right, why don't you explain these?

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:15.750
These show you leaving Sawaki's office.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:19.110
That incident is somehow 
connected, isn't it?

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.740
You think yakuza can produce

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:23.110
wrecking balls from thin air?

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:25.020
I'm asking the questions here!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:28.020
I was only there to deliver an order.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.800
And that exchange caused 
all this, didn't it?!

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:31.970
Sergeant...

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.480
May I have a moment?

00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:35.960
What is it?

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:37.940
What?

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:41.940
<i>Was that cream puff good?</i>

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:42.970
<i>Uh-huh.</i>

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:45.280
<i>Then, will you tell me now?</i>

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:49.210
<i>The older twin's name is Asahi, 
and the younger is Yonaga.</i>

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.280
<i>And what's your name?</i>

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:08.930
<i>The older twin's name is Asahi, 
and the younger is Yonaga.</i>

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.190
<i>And what's your name?</i>

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:18.940
<i>The older twin's name is Asahi, 
and the younger is Yonaga.</i>

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.730
<i>And what's your name?</i>

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:23.550
Can you slow it when she disappears?

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:24.150
Yes, sir.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:33.720
That's impossible!

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.200
It's true.

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:37.390
She disappeared right before my eyes.

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:39.670
The footage hasn't been 
altered in any way.

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:41.620
What about the twins?

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:45.200
There was a man calling himself 
their sponsor, so...

00:22:45.200 --> 00:22:46.620
You sent them with him?

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:47.910
Well...

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:51.240
They may be children, but you know 
how much trouble they caused!

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:52.990
I was following orders from above.

00:22:52.990 --> 00:22:53.720
What?

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:56.730
I was told not to pursue this case further.

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:06.880
You can go.

00:23:06.880 --> 00:23:09.110
You're being released due 
to lack of evidence.

00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:11.390
Your car's in the lot out back.

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:13.900
You want me to drive a wrecked car?

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:46.270
It's definitely my car, but the 
repairs were done fast.

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:48.390
Is this a free service?

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:51.530
We just came out and found it this way.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:53.230
You found it this way?

00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:54.860
That's right...

00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:57.540
The car and crash scene have 
been completely restored!

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:00.710
I'm the one who wants to ask what 
the hell happened, and how.

00:24:01.010 --> 00:24:03.520
Wrong way on a one-way street, 
ignoring a red light,

00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:05.840
speeding, property damage...

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:10.460
Normally, we'd hold you overnight 
to get the story out of you.

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:13.340
But there's no evidence at all.

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:19.310
<b>Image Data Not Found</b>

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:15.400
Huh?

00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:16.560
That's weird...

00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:19.310
We checked all the security
cameras in that area, too.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:21.360
But nothing was on them.

00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:21.810
Why are the pictures gone?

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:22.270
<b>Image Not Found</b>

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:22.310
<b>Isn't this crazy? 
Huge accident</b>

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:24.270
Several reports were filed.

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:22.810
<b>Isn't this crazy? 
Huge accident 

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:23.310
<b>Huge accident 

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:23.810
<b>There's no picture 

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>Huh? It was there a second ago 

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:25.810
Huh? What the...

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:27.120
And many witnesses were on the scene.

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:27.120
Sure you uploaded it?

00:24:27.120 --> 00:24:27.770
I did!

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:29.230
<b>Shinjuku  wrecking ball  girl  accident</b>

00:24:28.350 --> 00:24:32.530
But we didn't even find skid marks.

00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:33.490
Huh? Why isn't anything coming up?

00:24:33.490 --> 00:24:36.450
Nothing at the parking lot 
you said was destroyed,

00:24:36.820 --> 00:24:38.520
and no giant hole in the road.

00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:40.150
Impossible.

00:24:40.150 --> 00:24:43.580
It means you've been exonerated.

00:24:44.330 --> 00:24:45.460
Also...

00:24:45.910 --> 00:24:47.790
Forget what happened today.

00:24:48.340 --> 00:24:49.190
Got that?

00:24:51.550 --> 00:24:53.120
Your fine's been dropped.

00:24:53.120 --> 00:24:54.590
Just go home.

00:25:05.590 --> 00:25:08.520
The man who was with the Red Queen?

00:25:08.850 --> 00:25:09.790
Yes.

00:25:11.190 --> 00:25:14.820
<b>Kashimura Zoroku</b>

00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:12.680
What should we do?

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:16.330
Keep the old man, Kashimura, 
under surveillance, too?

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:18.140
No.

00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:20.780
If you look at the circumstances,

00:25:20.780 --> 00:25:23.320
he just seems to be caught up in it.

00:25:23.320 --> 00:25:26.790
For the time being, let's prioritize 
the Red Queen's capture.

00:25:29.250 --> 00:25:31.710
Feel free to eat all you like.

00:25:36.970 --> 00:25:39.140
<b>New and Used Cars 
We Buy and Sell</b>

00:25:36.970 --> 00:25:39.140
<b>Suzuki</b>

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.140
Huh? Are you serious?

00:25:39.140 --> 00:25:40.460
Yeah.

00:25:40.460 --> 00:25:43.470
All right, let me take a look...

00:25:44.030 --> 00:25:48.120
But, Kashimura-san, you really 
want to get rid of this car?

00:25:48.120 --> 00:25:49.180
Yeah.

00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:52.150
But you took such good care of it.

00:25:52.560 --> 00:25:54.620
I see no reason to scrap it.

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:57.600
Some weird stuff happened.

00:25:57.600 --> 00:25:58.870
Be careful with it.

00:25:58.870 --> 00:26:00.080
Right...

00:26:05.270 --> 00:26:06.490
Hey, it's me.

00:26:06.490 --> 00:26:09.810
Sorry. I ran into a little trouble.

00:26:11.470 --> 00:26:14.360
Sorry, but you two need to 
take care of things today.

00:26:14.360 --> 00:26:15.920
Give me a call if something comes up.

00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:19.140
<b>Kabukicho Ichibangai</b>

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:19.140
After I grab some food in 
Shinjuku, I'll head home.

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:22.340
Welcome!

00:26:24.280 --> 00:26:27.820
Beer, mutton stir-fry, and fried bread.

00:26:27.820 --> 00:26:28.710
Coming up.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:31.460
And I'll be using the ashtray.

00:26:31.460 --> 00:26:32.440
Help yourself.

00:26:40.290 --> 00:26:41.290
Your beer.

00:26:41.910 --> 00:26:43.070
Thanks.

00:26:54.160 --> 00:26:56.050
Don't they have cream puffs?

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.280
You pop up when and 
where you like, huh?

00:27:06.280 --> 00:27:07.870
Where'd you come from this time?

00:27:08.230 --> 00:27:09.730
Can I drink some of this?

00:27:10.090 --> 00:27:12.360
This isn't for kids to drink.

00:27:12.970 --> 00:27:15.500
Hey, bring me some orange juice.

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:17.500
Okay, got it!

00:27:20.900 --> 00:27:21.660
Well?

00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:23.350
What do you want?

00:27:23.890 --> 00:27:26.910
This is no place for a kid to hang around.

00:27:27.340 --> 00:27:29.400
I don't want any more trouble.

00:27:30.430 --> 00:27:32.000
Dreams of Alice.

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:33.880
Something from a manga again?

00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:37.130
That's what we're called.

00:27:37.950 --> 00:27:41.430
You can think of us as people 
with supernatural abilities.

00:27:42.110 --> 00:27:46.390
I don't know how such a thing 
comes to be, exactly.

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:53.100
But by using these visions called 
"Mirror Gates" as intermediaries,

00:27:53.100 --> 00:27:57.460
we have the ability to materialize 
any one thing we imagine.

00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:02.450
Chains or a bow and arrows...

00:28:02.450 --> 00:28:04.410
Some people can fix things, too.

00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:07.790
And that's the power you 
used to drive my car.

00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:10.620
That's right!

00:28:10.990 --> 00:28:14.180
It was my first time driving, 
but I learned how by looking—

00:28:14.180 --> 00:28:16.040
Here's your orange juice.

00:28:16.460 --> 00:28:19.800
And mutton stir-fry, with Chinese 
onions, and fried bread.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:27.680
Are you done talking?

00:28:28.100 --> 00:28:30.060
If you are, then please go home.

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:31.360
My food will get cold.

00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:32.850
I-I'm not done...

00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:35.730
I've decided that I like you!

00:28:35.730 --> 00:28:39.280
I'm going to make you my 
servant, Kashimura Zoroku!

00:28:39.510 --> 00:28:40.990
You'd better be happy!

00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:46.480
Don't stand on the chair.

00:28:46.480 --> 00:28:49.680
And keep your voice down 
in the restaurant!

00:28:49.680 --> 00:28:50.620
Yes, sir.

00:28:51.960 --> 00:28:53.280
Want some food?

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:53.830
Huh?

00:28:54.200 --> 00:28:56.320
In the convenience store, 
you were looking at dinners.

00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:57.880
When did you last eat?

00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:00.460
A-About three days ago...

00:29:01.070 --> 00:29:02.100
I'm fine.

00:29:02.530 --> 00:29:03.760
This long is nothing.

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:07.930
Hey!

00:29:08.610 --> 00:29:09.830
I need to place another order.

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:10.720
Sure!

00:29:16.570 --> 00:29:18.280
C-Can I really eat this?

00:29:18.280 --> 00:29:20.570
I don't have any money.

00:29:20.570 --> 00:29:22.320
Well, I do.

00:29:22.320 --> 00:29:24.490
Wow, check that out!

00:29:24.490 --> 00:29:26.850
Is she training for an eating 
contest or something?

00:29:24.490 --> 00:29:26.850
So good! So good!

00:29:27.530 --> 00:29:30.510
I didn't know food was this 
good in the outside world!

00:29:30.510 --> 00:29:32.780
How many servings are you gonna eat?

00:29:32.780 --> 00:29:34.260
I can't help it!

00:29:34.260 --> 00:29:37.890
Activating the Mirror Gate takes a 
tremendous amount of energy.

00:29:37.890 --> 00:29:39.090
It makes me hungry.

00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:42.430
Come to think of it, 
those twins were eating, too.

00:29:43.050 --> 00:29:45.200
Hold your chopsticks right!

00:29:46.130 --> 00:29:47.290
Chopsticks?

00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:49.600
You mean these things?

00:29:50.030 --> 00:29:51.820
You don't know how to use them?

00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:53.270
Lay off.

00:29:53.770 --> 00:29:56.270
It's my first time outside 
the research facility.

00:29:56.970 --> 00:30:00.260
Earlier, you said something 
about making a deal.

00:30:00.260 --> 00:30:02.350
What do you want me to do?

00:30:05.060 --> 00:30:06.780
Thank you very much!

00:30:07.870 --> 00:30:08.970
I want

00:30:09.550 --> 00:30:11.450
to crush the research facility.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:13.290
Research facility?

00:30:14.010 --> 00:30:17.360
There are many other Dreams 
of Alice, just like me.

00:30:17.360 --> 00:30:20.250
They're locked up there, and awful 
things are done to them.

00:30:22.060 --> 00:30:25.970
But even though I escaped, 
I couldn't do anything alone.

00:30:30.600 --> 00:30:31.720
I want your help.

00:30:32.020 --> 00:30:35.470
When I looked inside your head,
I saw that you're a good person.

00:30:37.750 --> 00:30:39.690
I want to help my friends!

00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:41.050
Please!

00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:49.410
<b>Free Information Desk</b>

00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:49.410
<b>The Most Information in One Place 
Safe, Easy Introductions to Any Shop</b>

00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:51.370
<b>Asano Beer 
Shanghai Home Cooking 
Shanghai Xiaochi</b>

00:30:49.800 --> 00:30:51.370
Thank you very much!

00:31:02.730 --> 00:31:03.880
Come with me.

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:06.910
We're going somewhere else.

00:31:13.390 --> 00:31:15.350
It's too bright...

00:31:15.350 --> 00:31:17.700
Don't just stand there. 
We'll get separated.

00:31:17.700 --> 00:31:19.410
Remember what I told you?

00:31:19.410 --> 00:31:23.770
This is no place for a kid to hang around.

00:31:23.770 --> 00:31:25.070
R-Right!

00:31:23.770 --> 00:31:28.030
Hotel Shinjuku

00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:43.330
<b>Shinjuku Diamond   VIP Diamond</b>

00:31:35.650 --> 00:31:38.610
Hi, Bro! How about a cabaret club?

00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:39.470
Hey, what kind of shop is that?

00:31:39.470 --> 00:31:41.320
When he said, "Bro," did he mean you?

00:31:41.320 --> 00:31:43.330
Just shut up and walk.

00:31:43.670 --> 00:31:47.080
Hey, wouldn't it be easier in your car?

00:31:47.080 --> 00:31:49.800
The car creeped me out, 
so I got rid of it.

00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:52.190
Creeped you out? Why?

00:31:52.190 --> 00:31:54.300
Would you just stop talking?

00:31:56.260 --> 00:31:59.730
<b>Hanazono Shrine</b>

00:31:57.990 --> 00:31:59.730
What's your name?

00:32:02.100 --> 00:32:03.740
Did you not hear me?

00:32:04.270 --> 00:32:06.100
You told me to stop talking.

00:32:06.100 --> 00:32:07.610
Well, now you can.

00:32:07.610 --> 00:32:08.650
What's your name?

00:32:09.120 --> 00:32:10.060
Sana.

00:32:10.610 --> 00:32:11.990
And your last name?

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:13.800
I don't know.

00:32:15.240 --> 00:32:17.830
I don't remember anything before 
the research facility.

00:32:18.370 --> 00:32:21.040
I don't even know where I came from.

00:32:21.320 --> 00:32:22.650
And "Sana" is

00:32:22.650 --> 00:32:25.380
just the name that Asahi 
and Yonaga gave me.

00:32:25.380 --> 00:32:27.230
Asahi and Yonaga?

00:32:27.650 --> 00:32:29.630
The twins who chased us.

00:32:29.870 --> 00:32:33.430
They were the only ones 
who called me by name.

00:32:33.890 --> 00:32:35.590
Yay! I got "very good luck"!

00:32:35.590 --> 00:32:37.550
Ugh, I got "very bad luck."

00:32:37.550 --> 00:32:40.110
Wow, I've never seen that before!

00:32:40.110 --> 00:32:41.520
Easy for you to say.

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:42.560
It'll be fine.

00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:44.980
I got "very good luck," so we 
can share half of each!

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:51.620
Only for a little while.

00:32:57.130 --> 00:33:00.980
For a little while, I'll give you 
food and a place to stay.

00:33:01.550 --> 00:33:03.730
But during that time,

00:33:03.730 --> 00:33:06.180
you'll help me with my work.

00:33:06.180 --> 00:33:08.150
One who does not work does not eat.

00:33:08.150 --> 00:33:08.840
Okay,

00:33:08.840 --> 00:33:10.170
that's fine!

00:33:10.170 --> 00:33:11.970
I knew you were a good—

00:33:11.970 --> 00:33:15.130
Show some respect for your elders!

00:33:12.300 --> 00:33:15.130
Ow, ow, ow!

00:33:17.310 --> 00:33:18.960
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:20.560
I won't baby you!

00:33:21.440 --> 00:33:22.860
And one other thing.

00:33:24.430 --> 00:33:26.870
Don't use that weird power again.

00:33:27.550 --> 00:33:28.480
Why not?

00:33:28.840 --> 00:33:30.920
With that, I can do anything.

00:33:30.920 --> 00:33:33.330
You don't want me to grant your wish?

00:33:33.330 --> 00:33:37.940
Earlier, you said you looked 
inside my head, right?

00:33:37.940 --> 00:33:39.930
Y-Yeah...

00:33:39.930 --> 00:33:41.240
So what?

00:33:41.480 --> 00:33:44.620
And you knew that I have 
a granddaughter, too.

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:46.310
See? Amazing, right?

00:33:48.730 --> 00:33:52.220
And you really don't understand 
what that means?

00:33:53.650 --> 00:33:56.640
You said you can do anything 
you can imagine, right?

00:33:56.640 --> 00:33:58.470
Y-Yeah.

00:33:59.600 --> 00:34:02.550
Then try using that power right here.

00:34:03.860 --> 00:34:05.270
Here?

00:34:05.640 --> 00:34:07.220
You can, right?

00:34:07.220 --> 00:34:09.610
Create chains or a wrecking 
ball or whatever.

00:34:09.610 --> 00:34:11.930
You'd cover this whole place in blood.

00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:16.300
You get it?

00:34:16.750 --> 00:34:18.970
Someone with a power like that

00:34:18.970 --> 00:34:22.030
mentioned a family member 
I hadn't even spoken of,

00:34:22.030 --> 00:34:24.370
and demanded that I make a deal.

00:34:24.660 --> 00:34:27.230
You blackmailed me.

00:34:27.230 --> 00:34:29.990
I... I didn't mean to...

00:34:31.010 --> 00:34:32.640
Even if you didn't,

00:34:32.640 --> 00:34:35.330
you can't know the intention 
of one who accepts.

00:34:36.340 --> 00:34:39.590
I have no interest in any deals or wishes.

00:34:40.290 --> 00:34:43.690
The only people anyone 
needs to think about

00:34:43.690 --> 00:34:45.480
are those within reach.

00:34:48.300 --> 00:34:49.300
Listen up!

00:34:49.300 --> 00:34:51.650
I hate crooked stuff!

00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:06.120
Listen.

00:35:06.120 --> 00:35:11.540
That research facility and its experiments 
are problems for grown-ups to solve.

00:35:11.540 --> 00:35:14.960
First, you need to fix that twisted 
temperament of yours.

00:35:15.620 --> 00:35:17.400
If you value your friends,

00:35:17.400 --> 00:35:19.930
they're all you need to think about.

00:35:21.570 --> 00:35:22.390
What?

00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:25.950
Nothing.

00:35:30.740 --> 00:35:33.830
You really don't know how 
to talk to people at all...

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:43.990
Yes, it's me.

00:35:45.860 --> 00:35:47.070
Understood...

00:35:47.540 --> 00:35:50.640
I'll head that way with the data now.

00:35:51.640 --> 00:35:53.980
Yes, see you soon.

00:36:03.880 --> 00:36:05.610
I'm sleepy...

00:36:05.610 --> 00:36:07.810
Not much longer. Hang in there.

00:36:09.250 --> 00:36:10.430
'Kay...

00:36:12.750 --> 00:36:16.070
This Wonderland created 
by the Red Queen is

00:36:16.070 --> 00:36:17.990
underneath the research facility.

00:36:18.600 --> 00:36:21.870
It's these children's playground, 
brought to life

00:36:21.870 --> 00:36:23.810
by randomly rewriting this space.

00:36:23.810 --> 00:36:25.690
She made this?

00:36:25.690 --> 00:36:27.370
I can't believe it...

00:36:29.330 --> 00:36:32.380
Next, please look at this.

00:36:33.620 --> 00:36:35.420
What are those things?

00:36:35.420 --> 00:36:36.770
Are they alive?

00:36:36.770 --> 00:36:38.730
Of course they are.

00:36:40.940 --> 00:36:45.510
She and the others made them from 
their favorite picture books.

00:36:45.890 --> 00:36:47.600
The principle is unclear.

00:36:48.120 --> 00:36:50.510
The space inside is intricately warped

00:36:50.510 --> 00:36:53.360
to be many thousands of times 
the size it originally was.

00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:55.230
And it's still growing.

00:36:55.520 --> 00:36:58.320
Is there anything here you understand?

00:36:58.320 --> 00:37:00.450
I can only say we're studying it now.

00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:02.990
Then, what will you do?

00:37:04.890 --> 00:37:06.800
There are two problems.

00:37:09.050 --> 00:37:10.230
The first is

00:37:10.230 --> 00:37:13.650
that the one possessing this 
immense power is a child.

00:37:13.650 --> 00:37:17.720
So if she remains in the outside world 
in a psychologically unstable state,

00:37:17.720 --> 00:37:21.630
the existence of the research facility 
could become publicly known.

00:37:22.070 --> 00:37:23.630
And the other is

00:37:23.630 --> 00:37:27.850
that the loss of the Red Queen, 
a valuable sample of this ability,

00:37:27.850 --> 00:37:33.180
is a massive detriment for us... 
no, for the country itself.

00:37:33.520 --> 00:37:35.550
And what do you intend to do?

00:37:36.740 --> 00:37:39.420
Her capture will be conducted in secrecy.

00:37:39.420 --> 00:37:45.140
But if an accident should bring this 
incident into public awareness...

00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:47.400
Coercion?

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:51.100
I would like you

00:37:51.100 --> 00:37:53.960
to recognize it as a state of 
emergency as soon as possible,

00:37:53.960 --> 00:37:56.310
and capture the Red Queen.

00:37:57.180 --> 00:37:57.930
Hey.

00:37:58.360 --> 00:37:59.210
Hey.

00:38:01.920 --> 00:38:03.050
Hey, wake up.

00:38:12.120 --> 00:38:14.050
Are we there?

00:38:14.050 --> 00:38:15.140
Not yet.

00:38:15.630 --> 00:38:16.680
Follow me.

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:26.280
Here we are.

00:38:26.610 --> 00:38:28.800
This is your house?

00:38:28.800 --> 00:38:30.120
Where I work.

00:38:30.700 --> 00:38:33.760
Thanks to you, I didn't get 
any work done today.

00:38:33.760 --> 00:38:35.950
So I had to let the young folks handle it.

00:38:38.090 --> 00:38:41.200
But I've gotta check how the 
prep is going, at least.

00:38:44.520 --> 00:38:46.130
Come in and wait a bit.

00:38:54.040 --> 00:38:55.500
Hey, is this...

00:39:09.860 --> 00:39:14.240
<b>For Friday's event</b>

00:39:12.490 --> 00:39:14.240
<b>For bouquet</b>

00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:24.710
Wow...

00:39:25.810 --> 00:39:27.960
Well, I'm a florist.

00:39:27.960 --> 00:39:29.260
A florist.

00:39:29.650 --> 00:39:33.220
I specialize in arrangements 
for events and gifts, though.

00:39:33.650 --> 00:39:35.050
Events?

00:39:35.050 --> 00:39:36.610
Gifts?

00:39:38.140 --> 00:39:40.240
Th-This flower is...

00:39:40.240 --> 00:39:41.790
Um...

00:39:41.790 --> 00:39:43.000
You know...

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:44.420
What is it?

00:39:44.420 --> 00:39:45.140
Uh...

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:47.950
It's called... block?

00:39:47.950 --> 00:39:50.320
No, that's wrong. What was it?

00:39:50.320 --> 00:39:53.780
Th-This flower is called ph-phlox.

00:39:54.120 --> 00:39:55.750
In the language of flowers...

00:39:55.750 --> 00:39:57.240
Uh...

00:40:08.110 --> 00:40:09.540
Take care, sir!

00:40:09.540 --> 00:40:10.670
Y-Yeah.

00:40:13.270 --> 00:40:17.140
Why is Sawaki-san all dressed up today?

00:40:17.140 --> 00:40:18.890
For this... This.

00:40:18.890 --> 00:40:19.600
Huh?

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:20.850
He's gonna cut off a finger?

00:40:20.850 --> 00:40:22.830
Idiot, it's for his girlfriend.

00:40:22.830 --> 00:40:25.270
His once-in-a-lifetime proposal.

00:40:25.270 --> 00:40:28.920
And he's bringing her a flower 
arrangement by Kashimura-san.

00:40:28.920 --> 00:40:29.710
Huh?

00:40:29.710 --> 00:40:31.490
So, that old guy this afternoon

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:33.430
really was a florist?

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:33.950
<b>Kashimura Floral</b>

00:40:36.990 --> 00:40:39.010
Sorry it's so late.

00:40:51.000 --> 00:40:53.050
Where are we going?

00:40:53.460 --> 00:40:54.620
Home.

00:40:55.080 --> 00:40:57.010
We have to walk more?

00:40:57.010 --> 00:40:58.930
You aren't even walking.

00:41:19.370 --> 00:41:21.750
<b>Kashimura    Zoroku  Sanae</b>

00:41:25.140 --> 00:41:26.180
Don't space out there.

00:41:26.180 --> 00:41:27.330
Upstairs.

00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:32.700
Take off your shoes.

00:41:45.930 --> 00:41:48.800
No one's using this room right now.

00:41:48.800 --> 00:41:51.230
It's a little dusty, but you'll 
have to make do.

00:41:53.000 --> 00:41:54.190
Go to sleep for the night.

00:41:55.120 --> 00:41:56.910
I'll get you some fresh clothes.

00:41:59.660 --> 00:42:01.500
Clothes?

00:42:04.720 --> 00:42:07.210
They're my granddaughter's, 
so they'll be big on you,

00:42:07.210 --> 00:42:07.950
but you can—

00:42:31.420 --> 00:42:33.100
Zoroku...

00:42:34.550 --> 00:42:36.830
Cream puff...

00:44:09.960 --> 00:44:14.960
Next Episode 
Dreams of Alice

00:44:11.450 --> 00:44:12.930
Dreams of Alice.
